          Clinician-guided care with medical director oversight · Compounded by [licensed pharmacy partner]
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proof-band" aria-label="Trust points">
      <span>Clinician-guided</span>
      <span>Personalized protocols</span>
      <span>Greenwood Village + Denver</span>
      <span>Licensed pharmacy fulfillment</span>
    </section>

    <section class="local-seo-band" aria-label="Local service area">
      <p>
        Eden Health Clubs serves Greenwood Village, the Denver Tech Center (DTC), Cherry
        Hills Village, Centennial, Englewood, Littleton, and the broader south Denver
        metro. The KLOW Stack is available through Eden's Greenwood Village health club or via telehealth for established
        Eden patients in Colorado.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="quick-answer-section" aria-labelledby="quick-answer-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Quick answer</p>
        <h2 id="quick-answer-heading">What is KLOW Stack peptide therapy at Eden?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="quick-answer-card">
        <p>
          The KLOW Stack at Eden Health Clubs is a clinician-guided peptide protocol in
          Greenwood Village that combines BPC-157, TB-500, KPV, and GHK-Cu to support
          recovery, gut barrier integrity, inflammatory balance, and skin/collagen health.
          Eligibility is determined during consultation with Eden's clinical team and
          medical director oversight.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Location:</strong> Greenwood Village, serving Denver, DTC, Cherry Hills, Centennial, Englewood, and Littleton.</li>
          <li><strong>Best fit:</strong> Active adults, longevity clients, GLP-1 clients, and aesthetic/recovery clients who want medical oversight.</li>
          <li><strong>Care model:</strong> Eden medical wellness club consult, licensed provider review, pharmacy fulfillment when prescribed.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--lead">
      <p class="eyebrow">Recovery + gut + skin + inflammatory balance</p>
      <h2>Effort is not the problem. Recovery is.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You train. You sleep. You eat well, or you try to. But somewhere in your late
          thirties or forties, something stopped matching. Recovery takes longer. Your skin
          does not bounce back the way it used to. Your gut is louder. Inflammatory
          discomfort lingers in ways it did not before.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is not a willpower problem. It is a repair-and-restoration problem, and most
          people are trying to solve it one supplement, one cream, one pill at a time, when
          the underlying systems are connected.
        </p>
        <p>
          The KLOW Stack is the protocol Eden uses when a client wants those systems
          addressed together: recovery, gut barrier, inflammatory balance, and skin, under
          a single clinician-guided plan.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What it is</p>
        <h2>What Is the KLOW Stack?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose prose--tight">
        <p>
          The KLOW Stack is a four-peptide protocol that combines BPC-157, TB-500, KPV,
          and GHK-Cu. Each peptide is studied for a distinct role: tissue repair, systemic
          recovery, inflammatory balance, and skin/collagen support. Together, they cover
          the parts of your physiology that recovery, aesthetics, and longevity all depend
          on.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Eden, the KLOW Stack is not sold as a kit. It is prescribed as a personalized
          protocol after clinical consultation, compounded by a U.S. licensed pharmacy
          partner, and adjusted based on your goals, history, and follow-up.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who it is for</p>
        <h2>For people who want clinician oversight, not research peptides ordered online.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Active adults in their 30s to 60s who feel recovery is not keeping pace with effort.</li>
        <li>Executives and high-performers managing systemic stress, fatigue, and inflammatory load.</li>
        <li>Aesthetic and longevity clients who want skin, gut, and recovery addressed in one protocol.</li>
        <li>Post-procedure clients looking for a structured tissue-repair conversation.</li>
        <li>Current GLP-1 clients who want to support recovery, skin elasticity, and lean-tissue maintenance.</li>
        <li>Clients who want medical guidance instead of internet self-experimentation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note-box">
        The KLOW Stack is not appropriate for everyone. Eligibility is determined during
        clinical consultation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ingredient-grid">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Inside the KLOW Stack</p>
        <h2>Four components. One connected repair system.</h2>
      </div>
      <article>
        <p class="ingredient-tag">Tissue Repair</p>
        <h3>BPC-157</h3>
        <p>
          Studied for its role in supporting the gut lining, tendon and ligament repair,
          and localized tissue recovery. Often described as the local repair peptide.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="ingredient-tag">Systemic Recovery</p>
        <h3>TB-500</h3>
        <p>
          A synthetic analog of a fragment of Thymosin Beta-4. Studied for its role in
          supporting systemic recovery, soft-tissue remodeling, and circulation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="ingredient-tag">Inflammatory Balance</p>
        <h3>KPV</h3>
        <p>
          A short tripeptide studied for its role in supporting inflammatory balance, gut
          barrier integrity, and skin inflammatory comfort.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="ingredient-tag">Skin & Collagen</p>
        <h3>GHK-Cu</h3>
        <p>
          A copper-binding peptide studied for its role in supporting collagen production,
          skin elasticity, and wound-area recovery.
        </p>
      </article>
      <p class="note-box note-box--wide">
        Why all four? Recovery, gut, inflammation, and skin are not separate problems.
        They are four windows into the same repair system. The KLOW Stack is the protocol
        Eden builds when a client wants all four addressed together rather than chasing
        each one alone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="process-section" id="how">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works at Eden</p>
        <h2>A premium protocol should feel clear from the first consult.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Consultation.</strong>
            A 30-45 minute visit with [Dr. NAME] or an Eden clinician to review your
            goals, history, and current protocols.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Medical review & eligibility.</strong>
            Your clinician determines whether the KLOW Stack is appropriate. Bloodwork may
            be requested.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Personalized protocol.</strong>
            Components, timeline, and support are tailored to your goals and labs, not
            pulled from a template.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Pharmacy fulfillment or in-club guidance.</strong>
            Compounded by [PHARMACY PARTNER], a U.S. licensed pharmacy. Optional in-club
            teaching is available for first-time users.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Follow-up & optimization.</strong>
            Check-ins help Eden adjust based on how your body responds and how the protocol
            fits into the rest of your care.
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why Eden</p>
        <h2>Eden is not an online peptide shop. It is a medical wellness club.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Real local health club: Greenwood Village, a physical address, and licensed providers on site.</li>
        <li>Functional medicine, aesthetics, recovery, and fitness under one roof.</li>
        <li>Premium environment designed for the south Denver longevity client.</li>
        <li>Clinician-guided protocols with medical director oversight.</li>
        <li>Integration with wellness injections, peptide injections, GLP-1 support, BHRT, recovery, fitness, and aesthetics.</li>
        <li>Personalized plans built around goals, labs, and the rest of your care.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="internal-link-grid" aria-label="Related Eden services">
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/">Functional Medicine</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/peptide-injections/">Peptide Injections</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/wellness-injections/">Wellness Injections</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/fitness-performance/">Fitness + Performance</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pricing-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h2>Know the right protocol before paying for the wrong one.</h2>
        <p>
          The KLOW Stack is a personalized protocol, not a product on a shelf. Your
          consultation determines whether it is the right fit, what components make sense
          for your physiology, and what level of clinical support your goals require.
          Pricing is reviewed during your consultation so you leave with a clear plan and a
          clear number.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button--primary" href="#consult-form">Book a Consultation</a>
    </section>

    <section class="testimonial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
        <h2>The real cost of waiting is another season of under-recovery.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-grid">
        <blockquote>Personalized protocols require clinical review, and consult availability with Eden's clinical team is limited each week.</blockquote>
        <blockquote>The clients who get the most out of KLOW are usually the ones who stopped self-experimenting and started a structured protocol.</blockquote>
        <blockquote>Recovery, skin response, gut comfort, and inflammatory balance are connected. Eden builds the plan around that connection.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
        <h2>Frequently asked.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqItems.map((item) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p>{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="split-section" id="consult-form">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start with a consultation</p>
        <h2>Stop guessing which protocol your body needs.</h2>
        <p>
          Eden will review your goals, current protocols, medications, and health history
          before recommending KLOW or a different path. If it is not the right fit, your
          clinician will tell you.
        </p>
        <p class="microcopy">
          Greenwood Village health club consults and telehealth follow-ups may be available for
          established Colorado patients.
        </p>
      </div>
      <LeadForm
        cta="Request My KLOW Consultation"
        service="KLOW Stack"
        page="KLOW Stack in Greenwood Village"
        leadSource="KLOW Stack Denver Landing Page"
        externalFormName="KLOW Stack Denver Lead Form"
        goalLabel="Goal / reason for inquiry"
        goalPlaceholder="Tell us what you are hoping to address."
        useTextarea
      />
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <p>
        Information on this page is educational and is not a substitute for personalized
        medical advice. Eligibility for the KLOW Stack is determined during clinical
        consultation. Results vary by individual. The peptides in this protocol may not be
        FDA-approved for all uses and are dispensed only when prescribed by a licensed
        medical provider and fulfilled by a licensed compounding pharmacy. Statements on this page have not been evaluated by
        the Food and Drug Administration. Eden Health Clubs makes no claims to diagnose,
        treat, cure, or prevent any disease.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="eden-action-bar" aria-label="Contact Eden">
      <a href="tel:+17206057678">
        <span>Phone</span>
        <strong>Call Now</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="mailto:care@edenhealthclubs.com">
        <span>Email</span>
        <strong>Care Team</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="#consult-form">
        <span>Consult</span>
        <strong>Book</strong>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </main>

  <script>
    const consultSection = document.querySelector("#consult-form");
    const actionBar = document.querySelector(".eden-action-bar");
    if (consultSection && actionBar) {
      const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
        ([entry]) => {
          actionBar.classList.toggle("is-hidden", entry.isIntersecting && entry.intersectionRatio >= 0.5);
        },
        { threshold: [0, 0.5, 1] }
      );
      observer.observe(consultSection);
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
